# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store

# --- Large media -----------------------------------------------------------
# Gameplay recordings: 612MB, and two of them are over GitHub's 100MB HARD
# per-file limit, so they cannot be pushed at all without Git LFS.
#
# Nothing at runtime needs them. They are development inputs for the offline
# smoke test (scripts/train_rl.py with no --live) and for
# scripts/check_perception.py; both take --video / --image and say so when the
# default is missing. Keep your copies locally.
media/testvideos/
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov

# Annotated frames written at runtime, regenerated on every debug run (~42MB).
debugOutput/

# --- Model output ----------------------------------------------------------
brawlstars_ppo*.zip
checkpoints/
checkpoints_*/
tb_logs/
*.tmp

# --- KEPT ON PURPOSE, do not add these --------------------------------------
# media/fixtures/                             committed calibration screenshots;
#                                             tests/conftest.py asserts on showdown.png
# media/gasphotos/                            5 labelled gas fixtures, ditto
# perception/*.npz                            digit templates, REQUIRED at runtime
# perception/username_classifier_weights.json trained weights, also required
# controls.example.json                       template for controls.json

# --- Development datasets ---------------------------------------------------
# Not needed to RUN the bot, only to RETRAIN via tools/. The trained artefacts
# they produce (perception/digit_*.npz, username_classifier_weights.json) are
# committed, so a fresh clone runs fine without these.
#
# Regenerating them needs gameplay recordings, which are not committed either:
#   media/crops + training_data  <- tools/make_training_data.py,
#                                   tools/harvest_digit_templates.py
#   media/testphotos             <- manual screenshots
#
# NOTE: these three lines used to carry trailing `# ...` comments. Git only
# treats `#` as a comment at the START of a line, so the comment text was part
# of the pattern and all three directories were silently NOT ignored -- 229 of
# the repo's 417 tracked files were development data nobody meant to commit.
# Sizes now live above the patterns instead of beside them.
#   media/crops/       17MB  username-classifier crops
#   training_data/     20MB  username-classifier dataset
#   media/testphotos/   9MB  manual calibration screenshots
media/crops/
training_data/
media/testphotos/
